,"kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Borůvka’s algorithm (JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BoruvkaMinimumSpanningTree"},{"type":"text","text":", NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"'boruvka'"},{"type":"text","text":"): in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each round every component takes its lightest edge to another component, under the strict"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (weight, position), so a round cannot close a cycle. The canonical minimum spanning"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forest of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the same edges as Kruskal’s, listed by round and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in an unspecified order within a round."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"boruvkaMinimumSpanningTree(weight:)"},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"SpanningTrees","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees","type":"topic"},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/GraphProtocols/Graph/primMinimumSpanningTree(from:weight:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Prim’s algorithm from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"root"},{"text":" (Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"prim_minimum_spanning_tree"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"root_vertex"},{"text":"): a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minimum spanning tree of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"root"},{"text":"‘s connected component only. Only that component’s edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are weighed.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Spanning